00:04:47.816 --> 00:04:51.556
The structure is a covered call against a $1,000 share position.

00:04:52.116 --> 00:04:56.696
Buy the shares at the next session's open, sell the nearest monthly out-of-the-money call,

00:04:56.936 --> 00:05:01.816
targeting roughly 1% of the underlying as premium, hold five sessions from entry,

00:05:02.356 --> 00:05:06.396
and exit at the fifth session's close or at the stop, whichever comes first,

00:05:06.396 --> 00:05:11.992
judged against the NASDAQ over those same five sessions, an 8% drop would

00:05:11.992 --> 00:05:17.132
trigger the stop and limit loss to $80 on that $1,000 share position before

00:05:17.132 --> 00:05:22.692
option premium. The target is plus 2% to 4% including premium collected while the

00:05:22.692 --> 00:05:27.332
broader market declines. If the next cybersecurity peer update revises earnings

00:05:27.332 --> 00:05:32.672
lower, the thesis is done. That is the invalidation, name before the money is at

00:05:32.672 --> 00:05:36.052
at risk, and we do not wait for the stop if that revision prints.

00:05:36.692 --> 00:05:40.792
At expiry, if shares sit below the strike, you keep the shares and the premium.

00:05:41.252 --> 00:05:46.172
If they sit above, the shares are called away and upside stops at the strike plus the premium.

00:05:46.852 --> 00:05:48.372
